cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Causari, cite the software with this file. A Survival Report
  has its own DOI (https://causari.dev/reports/survival/) and is cited on
  its own; the software and a report are different objects.
type: software
title: Causari
abstract: >-
  Measures how many lines from AI-tagged commits are still alive in a git
  repository, with the same repository's untagged lines as the baseline,
  and records the prompt, model and files behind every agent edit in a
  local, append-only ledger. Counts and intervals, not grades. Verifiable
  offline. This is Causari by Crovia Trust (causari.dev), not related to
  causari.ai or the npm scope @causari.
authors:
  - name: Crovia Trust
    email: info@croviatrust.com
    website: https://croviatrust.com
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/croviatrust/causari
url: https://causari.dev
keywords:
  - AI-generated code
  - code survival
  - git blame
  - provenance
  - software engineering measurement
  - Model Context Protocol
references:
  - type: generic
    title: Causari method (detection rules, computation, limits)
    url: https://causari.dev/method
    authors:
      - name: Crovia Trust
  - type: report
    title: Causari Survival Report (weekly series, one DOI per report)
    url: https://causari.dev/reports/survival/
    authors:
      - name: Crovia Trust
